 "applies_to": "Condair RO-E and RO-E+ reverse osmosis water treatment units for humidifier feed water.",
 "summary": "The Condair RO-E makes demineralised water for humidifiers. Its Integrated Controller exposes BACnet IP and MS/TP on-board with status, maintenance and disinfection countdowns, inlet/tank/membrane pressures, permeate quality and flow, valve states and writable tank pressure start/stop limits.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP",
  "BACnet MS/TP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": 1001,
 "access_inferred": false,
 "notes": [
  "BACnet is built into the Integrated Controller (RJ45 for BACnet IP, RS485 for MS/TP master or slave); it ships with the BACnet protocol set to Off.",
  "Factory Node ID (device instance) is 1001 and the MS/TP MAC is 127; BACnet IP uses UDP 47808 and supports registering with a BBMD.",
  "Some points are RO-E+ only or optional on the RO-E (permeate conductivity, drain valve, permeate valve).",
  "Pressure, temperature and flow units follow the controller's Metric/Imperial setting."
 ],
 "source": {
